From: Zack Maril <zmaril@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:34:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Add an `analysis_interfaces` query

Splits the analysis that `analysis` runs into two parts: everything up to
and including the item interface checks (well-formedness, coherence),
which is now the `analysis_interfaces` query, and type-checking function
bodies. `analysis` runs `analysis_interfaces` first, so nothing changes in
what runs or in what order.

This gives a point at which the crate's interface is known to be checked
but no function body has been, which `-Zearly-metadata` writes metadata
at. The `type_check_crate` timer of the analysis pass is now
`type_check_crate_interfaces` and `type_check_crate_bodies`;
`rustc_hir_analysis::check_crate` still runs both, for `-Zunpretty`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011C4oUhyTKGLkWYDeejZv2e
